 (386, 'Let us think and reflect – I (Extracts)', [
  'Extract 1: i. careful and secretive ii. It shows he trusts Gopi and hands over a special power quietly, without anyone noticing; it marks the start of her magical journey. iii. … wants the brush to help the needy and not to increase the greed of the rich. iv. A. The Magic Brush’s Secret (B also possible).',
  'Extract 2: i. … magical/miraculous powers (wonderful results). ii. Because the things painted by the brush became real – they were benefits gained by magic. iii. B is false. Correct: The Zamindar orders (commands) Gopi to paint a grand fortress and jewels. iv. He is greedy, proud, power-hungry and selfish.']),
 (387, 'Let us think and reflect – II', [
  '1. She kept her promise to the man; the Zamindar was already rich and wanted more wealth and power; painting for him would increase greed and injustice.',
  '2. It was a clever, non-violent threat to protect herself and stop the chase – she did not actually hurt anyone. I would also have painted something to block them, like a tall wall, or painted a gift to change his heart.',
  '3. It shows the victory of good over greed; she shares her joy with the people she served; it highlights unity and community happiness.',
  '4. Gopi used it selflessly for the poor (food, clothes, tools); the Zamindar would have used it selfishly for a fortress, treasures and power to rule the land.',
  '5. She is honest, brave, determined, loyal to her promise and kind; she is not afraid of power.',
  '6. The title is apt – the brush is magical and makes the dreams of poor villagers come true; Gopi’s dream of helping others is fulfilled.',
  '7. (Sample) I would paint schools, hospitals, clean water and trees for poor villages, and food for hungry people.',
  '8. She loves drawing and is lost in her imagination; it shows she is creative, artistic and a little playful/carefree.',
  '9. The poor need help to meet basic needs; the rich already have enough – the brush could make them greedier and misuse it.',
  '10. Her paintings gave food, warmth, tools and comfort; values of kindness, generosity, sharing and selfless service are highlighted.',
  '11. She painted a road and a horse to escape, a river to block the chasers and only threatened with a beast. Message: intelligence and peaceful wisdom are stronger than force.']),
