 (392, 'Let us write – Imaginative essay (sample)', [
  'THE SCARF THAT FLEW AWAY | One windy morning in Gudur, I was a bright red scarf drying on Lakshmi’s clothesline. Suddenly a strong gust lifted me high into the sky!',
  'I floated over green paddy fields, the busy Nellore bus stand and the blue waves of the Bay of Bengal. A seagull tried to catch me, and the salty air tickled my threads.',
  'At last I landed on a school gate. A little girl who was shivering in the cold picked me up and wrapped me round her neck. I felt warm and useful for the first time.',
  'In the evening she saw Lakshmi searching and returned me with a smile. The most valuable experience was learning that honesty and kindness can make even a small scarf feel proud.']),
